    "Performance": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "What the paper measured about its own assay. Reported, never scored.\n\nA limit of detection is a wet-lab sensitivity measurement on an isolate or a\ndilution series, and this project does not model sensitivity -- the Leetz 2007\nheld-out case turns on exactly that distinction. So nothing here enters a\nverdict. It is kept because a reader comparing two assays on the same target\nasks for it immediately, and because an efficiency far from 100% is a reason\nto read an entry's other numbers more carefully.",
      "properties": {
        "dynamic_range": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
