    "SpeciesSize": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One product-length band this assay gives for one species, as measured.\n\nFor an assay that identifies the species by product length rather than by\ndetecting one target, the length IS the readout, so it belongs here as\nnumbers rather than in a curator note as prose. Measured from GenBank\nrecords by scripts/measure_species_sizes.py, never copied from the paper:\non ATI the paper's stated sizes differ from the measured ones by 1-32 bp\n(see that entry's needs_review).\n\nA species can have more than one band \u2014 monkeypox clade I near 1067 bp and\nclade IIb near 1538 \u2014 so several rows may share a taxid. Bands from\ndifferent species may overlap, because they genuinely do, and that is the\nlimit of what a length can tell you: on ATI, vaccinia 1587-1615 and cowpox\n1598-1601 are not separable by size, which is why the design paper also ran\nan XbaI digest.",
      "properties": {
        "bp": {
          "items": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "maxItems": 2,
          "minItems": 2,
          "title": "Bp",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "n_records": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "N Records",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "note": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Note"
        },
        "taxid": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Taxid",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "taxid",
        "bp",
        "n_records"
      ],
      "title": "SpeciesSize",
      "type": "object"
    },
